# Code owners: a second line of defense for the maintainer lane of .github/merge-policy.json.
#
# With "Require review from Code Owners" on in the ruleset for main, a pull request that
# touches an owned path needs a code owner's approval. The last matching line wins, and a
# pattern without an owner means "no owner". The required merge-policy status applies the
# full policy, including what this file cannot express (new files only, size caps), so
# existing goldens, bench tasks, corpus files and images are left unowned here on purpose.
# When the lanes change in merge-policy.json, change this file in the same pull request;
# scripts/automerge/workflows.test.ts checks that every maintainer-lane glob has an owner.

# 1. Every path needs a maintainer's approval by default (maintainer lane).
*                         @NeuralDEEPnet

# 2. Auto-lane paths: no owner, so GitHub asks for no approval.
*.md
/docs/
/examples/
/bench/tasks/
/corpora/
/lib/

# 3. Back to the maintainer lane: code, scripts, binaries and build files in any folder,
#    including the auto-lane folders above.
